        "content": "# AI Assessment Pipeline\n\nOwned By: Diego Alvarez\nLast Updated: 09/23/2026\n\nProduction-grade pipeline that validates FastAPI/Ollama availability, submits a task for AI-driven automation assessment, persists the validated result to MongoDB, and indexes it for semantic search — with centralized error notification at every failure point.\n\n## Expected Flow\n1. ReceiveAssessmentTaskRequest: Webhook entry point that receives the task description\n2. GetFastAPIHealthStatus: Checks FastAPI/Ollama service availability\n3. ValidateFastAPIHealth: Confirms the health check reports a healthy status\n4. ValidateTaskPayload: Confirms the incoming webhook payload is well-formed before sending\n5. PostAssessmentRequest: Submits the task to the AI assessment service\n6. ValidateAIAssessment: Confirms the AI returned a non-empty, valid assessment\n7. FormatAssessmentDocument: Structures the assessment for storage\n8. SaveAssessmentMongoDB: Persists the final assessment document\n9. IndexAssessmentInVectorStore: Calls the subworkflow that embeds and indexes the assessment in Qdrant for similarity search\n\n## Resiliency & Error Handling\n- Retry on Fail: enabled on HTTP Request nodes to absorb transient network/timeout issues\n- Centralized Alerts: every failure branch (health, payload, request, assessment, format, save, indexing) calls the notifyError subworkflow instead of duplicating Slack logic\n- Severity Tiering: critical for infra/data-loss risks (unreachable service, failed save), warning for recoverable/business-logic issues (invalid payload, empty assessment, indexing failures)\n- Global Error Trigger: configured at workflow settings level to catch unanticipated node failures outside the explicit IF branches",
        "height": 688,
        "width": 1568,
        "color": 6
      },
